unit newVMTests;

{*******************************************************************************

     FPCUnit test suite for the five TVMobj* types (newVM.pas, newVMSingle.pas,
     newVMComplex.pas, newVMComplexSingle.pas, newVMI.pas).

     One TTestCase per type - TVMobjTests / TVMobjSTests / TVMobjZTests /
     TVMobjCTests - covering: construction and dimension validation, Element
     get/set (including out-of-range and the non-square addressing that
     calcoffset* used to get wrong), writeMatrix, fillRandom, Id, DataPtr
     (real types only), CopyObj* independence, MatMult*, LinearSolve*, Invert*,
     every operator overload (+, -, unary -, *, /, =) including the assertion
     paths, and the elementwise VML functions (Sin/Cos/Tan/Sinh/Sqr/Sqrt/Exp/Ln).
     The two complex types additionally cover RealToComplex*/GetRealPart*/
     GetImagPart*/SplitComplex*, EigDecompose* (verified via A*v = lambda*v,
     not hard-coded eigenvectors, since LAPACK doesn't guarantee a particular
     sign/normalisation), and the mixed real/complex operators.

     TVMobjITests (newVMI.pas, integer index array/matrix) covers the same
     "core object shape" subset - construction, Element get/set, writeMatrix,
     fillRandom (now bounded: TVMobjI.fillRandom takes explicit loBound/
     hiBound, unlike the fixed N(0,1) fillRandom on the other four types),
     Id, DataPtr, CopyObjI, plus Transpose and linspace - but none of
     MatMult/LinearSolve/Invert/operators/VML functions, since newVMI has no
     equivalents (BLAS/LAPACK/VML don't operate on plain integers).

     TVMobjCLTests (newVMCL.pas, GPU-resident single via OpenCL+clFFT) - a
     SIXTH TTestCase, deliberately not mentioned alongside the five above:
     it covers the same "core object shape" subset as TVMobjSTests
     (construction incl. the Create(r,c,Values) convenience overload,
     Element get/set, writeMatrix, fillRandom, Id, CopyObjCL, Transpose,
     linspace, every operator overload, the elementwise Sin/Cos/Tan/Sinh/
     Sqr/Sqrt/Exp/Ln functions, MatMultCL) PLUS ToDevice/ToHost (the
     TVMobjS bridge TVMobjCL alone has) and FFT/IFFT (via clFFT - TVMobjS
     itself has no FFT; this is closer to newVMComplex.pas's own FFT/IFFT
     in spirit, just GPU-side) - but explicitly NOT LinearSolveCL/InvertCL
     or any of Kron/Diag/Trace/Det/Flip*/Merge*/Reshape/Repmat/AddScalar/
     SubMatrix/DCT/DST, none of which newVMCL.pas implements - see that
     unit's own header comment (SCOPE) for why. Gated on HAVE_OPENCL
     (newVMConfig.inc, generated by newvmconfigure - see that tool's own
     header comment) end to end: the uses clause below, the class
     declaration, its implementation, and its RegisterTest call are ALL
     inside one {$IFDEF HAVE_OPENCL}, so a machine where newvmconfigure
     didn't find both OpenCL.dll and clFFT.dll never references
     newVMCL.pas at all - the test count and "N:262 E:0 F:0" summary style
     newVMtest.lpr already reports simply excludes these tests cleanly,
     the same "probe once at config time, degrade gracefully" contract
     PUREPASCAL/HAVE_FFTW/etc already establish for the other four units,
     rather than registering tests that would need their own runtime
     skip/pass-vacuously logic.

     TVMobjMTLTests (newVMMetal.pas, GPU-resident single via Metal +
     MetalPerformanceShadersGraph) - a SEVENTH TTestCase, the Metal analogue
     of TVMobjCLTests immediately above: same coverage, same scope, same
     {$IFDEF HAVE_METAL}-end-to-end gating (this time from newvmconfigure's
     Apple-Silicon-only Metal+MPSGraph probe), for newVMMetal.pas's TVMobjMTL
     instead of newVMCL.pas's TVMobjCL. See newVMMetal.pas's own header
     comment for why this is a new, parallel unit rather than a change to
     newVMCL.pas itself.

     Run via the console test runner in newVMtest.lpr.

*******************************************************************************}

{$mode objfpc}{$H+}

{$I newVMConfig.inc}

